<p>Whether you&rsquo;re a new user or a seasoned pro, ScreenCastsONLINE offers in-depth screencasts on a wide range of topics, from tutorials to app discovery. <a href="https://screencastsonline.com/members/aff/go/bterpstra">Check it out.</a></p>

<dl>
  <dt><a href="https://cloak.aside0.com/">Cloakshot</a></dt>
  <dd>Cloakshot by Spawn Lau is a screenshot redaction app for iPhone, iPad, and Android (works on Mac just fine). Scan and edit on your device; export with an eligible trial or one-time Pro purchase.</dd>
  <dd>
    <p>I use CleanShot X for most of my redaction work, but the automatic scanning and simplified redaction in Cloakshot works really well and could be a real timesaver if you share a lot of images that need redaction.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt><a href="https://smolmac.com/">Smol</a></dt>
  <dd>Really solid neural image compression and conversion, now with an extensive CLI for integrating into workflows. In their public 24-image benchmark, Smol’s AVIF was 15–21% smaller than Apple’s at the same quality score. 100% local, $29 once.</dd>
  <dt><a href="https://genjuxapps.com/apps/nautilus/index.html">Nautilus</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Nautilus is a free, native iOS reader for Hacker News. On-device AI thread summaries, a private briefing, Story Rules, Radar watchlists, offline reading, and hand-tuned Editions — no ads, no tracking, no account required.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>This is really nice. I never could keep up with Hacker News very well.</p>
  </dd>
